      "description": "Watch Panathinaikos vs CSKA 1948 highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 5, 2026. The UEFA Europa Conference League provided a high-stakes encounter on 2026-08-05 as Panathinaikos hosted CSKA 1948. Both sides took to the pitch knowing that tactical discipline and clinical finishing would be the deciding factors in this prestigious European competition. Clinical Finishing Defines the Opening Period The match ignited early as CSKA 1948 looked to exploit spaces in the home side's defensive line. Their persistence was rewarded in the 21st minute when Santino Andino Valencia delivered a pinpoint assist to Adriano Jagusic , who calmly slotted the ball home to break the deadlock. Panathinaikos struggled to regain their composure, and things went from bad to worse just ten minutes later. In the 31st minute, Hector Cuellar turned provider, setting up Georgi Rusev for a clinical finish that doubled the visitors' lead and left the home crowd stunned heading into the halftime break. Defensive Resilience and Tactical Battles As the second half got underway, Panathinaikos introduced fresh energy with substitutions including Vicente Taborda and Anass Zaroury in an attempt to claw their way back into the game. The contest grew increasingly physical, leading to yellow cards for Hector Cuellar and Triantafyllos Tsapras as both teams fought for every inch of grass. Despite late pressure and further changes from the bench, the CSKA 1948 backline remained organized and resolute. The final whistle at 90+4 minutes confirmed a hard-fought performance that saw the visitors secure all three points through a professional display of football."
